{"id": "unknown-2026-07-27-004", "date": "2026-07-27", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 7, "week": 31, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["cotton_price", "supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Weekly price shock alert: BCI cotton - week ended July 24", "content": "BCI cotton prices split across Asia in the week ended July 24, with Pakistan's KCA spot rate up 1.07 per cent, China's 3128B up 0.62 per cent and India's Shankar-6 flat.\nThe divergence changes raw-cotton cost visibility for mills, yarn exporters and apparel sourcing teams.\nIndian yarn may offer steadier quotes; Pakistan and China need closer checks on cotton buying and yarn pass-through.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/weekly-price-shock-alert-bci-cotton-week-ended-july-24-312095-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
